{
  "_note": "Muskellunge (Esox masquinongy), the legendary \"fish of ten thousand casts\" of Midwest lakes. Markings from field-guide descriptions: shaped like a pike but bigger, light silvery-olive to bronze with DARK bars or spots on a light ground (a pike is the reverse), fins and dorsal set far back, and sharply pointed tail lobes. From above, as seen from a boat, the shape is exaggerated: a flat duck-bill snout narrower than the head, the dorsal and anal fins showing near the tail. The dorsal and anal fins are solid wedges and the tail a lens, so they show from above too. 950 mm long, the base length (SECOND-ORDER R1.150-R1.169).",
